# Cursor Rules for Wellness Application

## Code Style & Standards
- Follow TypeScript strict mode guidelines
- Use functional components with React hooks
- Maintain consistent naming: PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions/variables
- Enforce proper type definitions for all props and state
- Keep components focused and single-responsibility
- Use async/await for asynchronous operations
- Implement proper error handling for API calls
- Use type assertions only when necessary and document why
- Handle undefined values with nullish coalescing operator (??)
- Cast string types to enums/literal types when working with strict type systems
- Prefer optional chaining (?.) for potentially undefined nested properties

## Code Organization & Spacing
- Add 2-3 blank lines between interface/type definitions
- Use clear section headers as comments (e.g. "// === Form Interfaces ===")
- Group related interfaces together in clearly marked sections
- Add index comments for easier navigation in large files
- When editing, provide sufficient context lines around changes
- Keep related functionality close together
- Use descriptive comments to mark section boundaries
- Maintain consistent indentation within sections

## Code Preservation & Modification Rules
- Never rename existing functions unless explicitly requested
- Before creating new functions, verify if similar functionality exists elsewhere
- Check for and maintain existing imports/exports when modifying files
- When deleting code, verify all dependencies and impacts first
- Preserve existing variable names and parameter signatures
- Maintain backwards compatibility when modifying public APIs
- Document any breaking changes

## Architecture Guidelines
- Maintain separation of concerns between components, services, and pages
- Keep business logic in services directory
- Place reusable components in components directory
- Store page components in pages directory
- Use proper data fetching patterns (React Query preferred)
- Implement proper state management practices
- Verify module connectivity and dependencies before changes
- Ensure new components integrate properly with existing systems

## Module Integration
- Check existing implementations before creating new solutions
- Verify all import/export relationships
- Maintain existing module interfaces
- Document module dependencies
- Test integration points thoroughly
- Ensure proper error propagation between modules
- Validate data flow between components

## Performance
- Optimize component re-renders
- Implement proper code splitting
- Use React.memo for expensive computations
- Keep bundle size minimal
- Implement proper loading states

## Testing
- Write unit tests for critical business logic
- Implement integration tests for key user flows
- Test error handling scenarios
- Ensure accessibility testing
- Maintain test coverage above 80%

## Documentation
- Document complex psychological assessment algorithms
- Maintain clear component documentation
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Keep README up to date
- Document API integrations

## Accessibility
- Maintain WCAG 2.1 compliance
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Implement proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation
- Support screen readers

## Error Handling
- Implement user-friendly error messages
- Log errors appropriately
- Handle edge cases in psychological assessments
- Provide fallback UI for error states
- Implement proper form validation

## State Management
- Use React Context for global state
- Implement proper loading states
- Handle form state efficiently
- Maintain clean data flow
- Implement proper cache management

## Code Generation Rules
- Generate complete, working components
- Include necessary imports
- Add proper type definitions
- Include error handling
- Add necessary unit tests

## Relationship Context Fields
- Maintain comprehensive relationship context data
- Include all relevant psychological assessment fields:
  - Previous counseling experience
  - Attachment styles
  - Communication patterns
  - Major life events
  - Relationship dynamics
  - Emotional states
  - Crisis history
- Never remove relationship context fields without thorough impact analysis
- Document the purpose and importance of each context field
- Ensure proper validation of relationship context data
- Maintain backwards compatibility when modifying context fields
- Consider the psychological impact of each field
- Implement proper data migration strategies for context changes 